    perf(frontend): every page is its own chunk — the entry bundle drops 3.4 MB → 0.9 MB
    
    Eighteen routes rode in one entry chunk: the first paint of ANY screen paid
    for all of them. The nine page components load through lazyPage() now — each
    becomes its own chunk fetched on first navigation (vite splits the shared
    hooks out on its own), and the Suspense sits INSIDE the shell so the nav,
    banners and queue dock stay put while a page chunk is in flight.
    
    lazyPage also owns the failure mode code splitting creates here: Update &
    restart swaps dist/ under an open tab, whose old index.html then requests
    chunk files that no longer exist. First failed chunk load = one reload (the
    new index.html carries current chunk names); a sessionStorage flag stops a
    reload loop when the chunk is missing for a real reason, and clears on any
    successful load so the next update gets its one reload too.
    
    Measured: entry 3 460 kB → 901 kB (gzip 295 kB); DatasetPage 594 kB,
    GuidePage 332 kB, BankPage 293 kB… load only when visited. Probe rerun on
    all four pages through real lazy navigation: 0 findings.
